00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.010 align:start position:0%
 
foreign  the Fourth of July is one of the busiest  holidays for air travel across the  United States  from coast to coast millions of  Americans will take to the skies in the  next few days  and this year it's shaping up to be even  busier as the aviation sector slowly  returns to its pre-pandemic levels  but it's the increasing cost of living  that's got many people worried I like to  travel every weekend but unfortunately  with inflation it's kind of hard to do  that I had to get back to see family I  haven't seen them since covid so it  really Wilson  a question we just had to do it but we  won't be going away for the rest of  Summer that's it now yeah for some  reaching their destination this weekend  with their hard-earned tickets is  proving more challenging I was flying  with Delta and they canceled my flight  as I'm boarding a plane our flight got  canceled yesterday so now we're  hopscotching around to get home we  actually got five  day out of Heathrow they canceled 30  flights so we've got a message from  United at quarter to midnight and we  were supposed to be flying at 8am in the  morning we were stranded two young  children  what do you think  the issue bad weather air traffic delays  and stopping shortages  and it's not just in the U.S airports  across Europe and the UK are struggling  to readjust after many workers left  their jobs during the pandemic  and many more went on strike in response  to the soaring costs of living  some countries like Germany have  launched schemes to bring in temporary  foreign workers Heathrow this morning  was an absolute mess  we were at the we were told to arrive  five hours before the flight to make  sure that we got on our flight and we  were just queuing the desk when open we  were just queuing the Keyser outside it  is horrendous there  back in the U.S with thousands of flight  cancellations and delays some airlines  are giving out bonuses for flight  attendants to ramp up Staffing others  are offering Pilots triple pay to pick  up extra trips  and for those left stranded they get  waivers to change their tickets for free  for those who prefer to skip the airport  during this busy holiday driving to  their destination seems to be a good  option  but with some of the highest gas prices  on record that may also prove costly  Jillian wolf Al Jazeera

